<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Omaheke</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Omaheke is a sandveld region of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/namibia">Namibia</a> on the edge of the Kalahari, now an administrative region with its capital at Gobabis. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-waterberg">Battle of Waterberg</a> in 1904 German troops drove the Herero into this waterless land and sealed it off, and many thousands died of thirst, a central episode of the Herero and Nama <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genocide">genocide</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/omaheke.jpg" alt="Omaheke" width="320" height="308" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NordNordWest · CC BY-SA 3.0 de · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Omaheke_in_Namibia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
